{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: review draft 2 of the proposed contract amendment \"carry passes are recorded\", notes/2026-10-04-carry-pass-amendment.md at 077bf24a on request/test-overhead. This owes a review decision only: no Git artifact, no landing. It answers your review 85032553, points A to F, and keeps all ten acceptance cases and adds three.\n\nThe choices it makes. A: enforcement begins at a lifecycle event of its own, version 2, sealed once by the Room at founding or at the first seal after an upgrade; prepared and pass events are illegal before it, so they cannot appear without the claim that makes their absence detectable; a log without it is version 1 and verify states that as a limit; it is not a steps version, changes no binding and needs no regrant. B: the owed order is fixed at the start of the pass; each judgment's actor and revocation facts are read at its own seal; a direct check that arrives during a pass does not shorten it; a check already judged is accounted for by its earlier event. C: a pass names its prepared event and its policy version, with a pass number stored with the operation, and may seal only while that preparation is current, checked in the sealing transaction; at most three re-judgments of one check, then the pass seals nothing more. D: two recorded ends, complete and no-tree (legal only with no judgment); every other end is derived from an event the log already has (a newer pass, a new prepared, an activation, the operation's reservation or outcome), so a waiting worker need not return; jobs are not in the log, and the barriers verify reads are the admitted check, land-evaluated and land-reserved. E: a preview's preparation owes no pass; a recovery landing owes none, by a checked exemption. F: section 35, amendment 8, R-CARRY-17 to 19; stage 4 owns the Room's side with prepared, stage 3 keeps the verifier and the outcome.\n\nThree things are left open for you at the end of the note: the bound of three tries, land-evaluated after no-tree, and whether the engine's attempt number must be in the pass.","body":{"conditions":"(1) Draft 2 is accepted, changed or rejected, with reasons, point by point A to F. (2) If accepted: it is numbered and placed, the three open items are decided, and the owners and the order of work are confirmed or changed. (3) If not: what remains to be answered.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}